# Screen Patterns

## Navigation Typing

Screens receive typed navigation props from React Navigation:

```tsx
type Props = NativeStackScreenProps<HomeStackParamList, 'AttendanceManagement'>;
export function AttendanceManagementScreen({ navigation }: Props) { ... }
```

Route types defined in `src/navigation/types.ts`.

## Standard Screen Layout

**Tab-visible stacks** (Home, Settings list): match `SettingsScreen` — do **not** use bottom safe-area edge (tab bar already has inset). See `src/constants/tabScreenLayout.ts` and `context/company.md`.

```tsx
import {
  TAB_SCREEN_SAFE_AREA_EDGES,
  TAB_SCREEN_SCROLL_PADDING_BOTTOM,
} from '@src/constants/tabScreenLayout';

<SafeAreaView style={styles.safe} edges={TAB_SCREEN_SAFE_AREA_EDGES}>
  <View style={styles.stackHeader}>
    <HeaderBackButton onPress={() => navigation.goBack()} tintColor={colors.primary} />
    <Text style={styles.stackHeaderTitle}>{t('...')}</Text>
  </View>
  <FlatList
    contentContainerStyle={{ paddingBottom: TAB_SCREEN_SCROLL_PADDING_BOTTOM }}
    ...
  />
  <StatusAlert {...statusProps} />
</SafeAreaView>
```

Full-screen modals may use `edges` including `'bottom'`. Face capture: see `context/face-enroll.md`.

## Data Loading Pattern

Use custom hooks for paginated API data:

```tsx
const { employees, counts, loading, refreshing, error, refresh, loadMore, retry } =
  useAttendanceList({ companyId, fromDate, toDate, dayStatus, search, limit, onError });
```

- `loading` — initial load; `loadingMore` — pagination; `refreshing` — pull-to-refresh
- Pass `onError` callback for error display via `presentError()`
- Guard against `companyId == null` (show "select company" message)

## Authentication Context

```tsx
const { selectedCompany } = useAuth();
const companyId = selectedCompany?.id ?? null;
```
